      "title": "Somalia : Acute Malnutrition",
      "description": "Global Acute Malnutrition (GAM) is the presence of both moderate acute malnutrition (MAM) and severe acute malnutrition (SAM) in a population. Height and body weight ratios are measured for children between 6 months and 5 years old to determine the prevalence of malnutrition. Rates above 15 per cent are ordinarily considered an emergency but rates above 30 per cent contribute to the case for famine in a given area.. [Source: This metadata record was automatically extracted from the Humanitarian Data Exchange (HDX); Original dataset: https://data.humdata.org/dataset/somalia-acute-malnutrition-burden-and-prevalence]",
